n_level": "L1_architecture", "debug_lesson": "On this Ascend backend only plain-affine block indices lower to block DMA: `tl.minimum`/`tl.maximum` index clamps cost 70x (5.5-7.3 ms vs 0.078 ms) and 2-D strided tiles cost 130x (10.1 ms). Load count is nearly free (4/6/8 shifted loads all ~0.078 ms), so tiling decisions should target index-expression simplicity, not byte volume.", "strategy_evolution": "Started from the FlagGems seed (0.136). Moved to a self-contained pair of Triton kernels (flat last-axis kernel + generic (outer,3,inner) kernel) for a 0.4975 geo_mean baseline. Bounded microbenchmarks then redirected the effort from bandwidth/tiling toward (i) index-expression lowering and (ii) host dispatch overhead, which the device-side roofline alone would not have revealed.", "knowledge_assessments": []}}
